{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 66,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Make a joyful noise unto God, all the earth:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sing forth the glory of his name:\nMake his praise glorious.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Say unto God, How terrible are thy works!\nThrough the greatness of thy power shall thine enemies submit themselves unto thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All the earth shall worship thee,\nAnd shall sing unto thee;\nThey shall sing to thy name. [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Come, and see the works of God;",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "He is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " terrible in his doing toward the children of men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He turned the sea into dry land;\nThey went through the river on foot:\nThere did we rejoice in him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He ruleth by his might for ever;\nHis eyes observe the nations:\nLet not the rebellious exalt themselves. [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh bless our God, ye peoples,\nAnd make the voice of his praise to be heard;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who holdeth our soul in life,\nAnd suffereth not our feet to be moved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou, O God, hast proved us:\nThou hast tried us, as silver is tried.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou broughtest us into the net;\nThou layedst a sore burden upon our loins.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou didst cause men to ride over our heads;\nWe went through fire and through water;\nBut thou broughtest us out into a wealthy place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will come into thy house with burnt-offerings;\nI will pay thee my vows,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which my lips uttered,\nAnd my mouth spake, when I was in distress.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will offer unto thee burnt-offerings of fatlings,\nWith the incense of rams;\nI will offer bullocks with goats. [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Come, and hear, all ye that fear God,\nAnd I will declare what he hath done for my soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I cried unto him with my mouth,\nAnd he was extolled with my tongue.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I regard iniquity in my heart,\nThe Lord will not hear:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But verily God hath heard;\nHe hath attended to the voice of my prayer.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.66.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.66.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blessed be God,\nWho hath not turned away my prayer,\nNor his lovingkindness from me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ],
  "headings": [
    {
      "style": "s1",
      "text": "Praise for God’s mighty deeds and for his answer to prayer.",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "d",
      "text": "For the Chief Musician. A Song, a Psalm.",
      "before_verse": 1
    }
  ]
}
